[0.000, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[94m\r\n1.\u001b[93m stealc-v2-family-intel\u001b[97m (family-intel, new) — Candidate 2. Before saving I spot-verified its distinctive claims against the forum's solved threads:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nthe sRDI MZ-stub/reflective-loader ABE helper and Early-Bird APC injection (!79, !85), WinINet-not-WinHttp with decoy decrypted names (!125, !141),\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nnlohmann JSON builder (!127), CIS locale gate (!102), and ComputerName+UserName named event (!104) — all code-verified. Per the scoped-negative\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\ndiscipline, \"no RC4 on wire,\" \"no persistence,\" and \"no anti-VM\" are written as observations about the verified build, not family invariants.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nNamed/tagged with the family name as family-intel memories should be.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[94m\r\n2.\u001b[93m crt-fid-triage-of-detector-api-hits\u001b[97m (workflow, new) — Candidate 3. Generic FID-first triage rule for static-CRT MSVC binaries; includes the caveat\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nthat a CRT false positive clears only that call site, not the behavior.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[94m\r\n3.\u001b[93m pitfall-printable-xor-decode-of-arithmetic-tables\u001b[97m (pitfall, new) — Candidate 4. The self-similar printable run → STL popcount/pshufb table\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\npattern, with closed-form and xref-sweep verification steps; cross-referenced to the related existing pitfall mem-3d4ebcf8.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[94m\r\n4.\u001b[93m mem-c893fd1e\u001b[97m (technique, updated via overwrite) — Candidate 1's genuinely novel content (real key = short ASCII literal set into a std::string\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nglobal by a pre-main\u001b[93m _initterm\u001b[97m dynamic initializer; 100%-printable-yield confirmation standard) was folded into the existing keystream-reuse memory\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nsaved earlier this run.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[94m\r\n5.\u001b[93m initializer-lea-pair-scan-maps-string-globals\u001b[97m (technique, new) — Candidate 5. The RIP-relative LEA-pair scan of dynamic initializers to produce a\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nglobal→plaintext map that makes dynamically-resolved API identities byte-provable; cross-linked to mem-c893fd1e.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[36m\u001b[1m\r\n## Skipped\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\n-\u001b[1m Candidate 1 as a standalone memory\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[97m — its core claim (carved \"keys\" are single-key RC4 ciphertexts) duplicates mem-c893fd1e, the keystream-reuse\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nlesson already saved this run. Rather than create a near-duplicate, I merged its new details into that memory.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nThe curation decision record is posted on the forum as\u001b[93m #memory-library-curation\u001b[97m. No sample hashes, paths, decoded C2 values, or session specifics\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nwere saved into cross-run memory (the one deliberate exception: the\u001b[93m builder_v2\u001b[97m assert-path string and IElevator CLSIDs in the family-intel memory,\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nwhich are family-wide build artifacts documented as discriminators, not sample-unique facts).\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[32m\r\n●\u001b[39m\u001b[1X\u001b[90m\u001b[Cmain · ▸ finish() · 64 chars\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\n🤖\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[97m\r\nResuming analysis…\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[36m\r\n┌\u001b[1m Prompt \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[36m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\u001b[34;1H│\u001b[90mHow can Thorium help?                                                                                                                               \u001b[36m│\u001b[35;1H│\u001b[90m                                                                          